Rust Code Standards

- Prefer `cargo fmt` defaults; enforce `rustfmt.toml` settings if present.
- Require `clippy --all-targets --all-features -D warnings` on CI; fix lints proactively.
- Model ownership explicitly; avoid `clone()` unless the cost or semantics are justified in comments.
- Encapsulate unsafe code behind safe abstractions with thorough safety docs.
- Design APIs around traits and iterators; embrace `Result` and `Option` to make failure explicit.
- Keep functions cohesive and under ~30 lines; extract helpers and modules instead of deep nesting.
- Write unit tests alongside code, integration tests in `tests/`, and property tests when invariants matter.
- Prefer `Arc` over `Rc` in async contexts; document Send/Sync guarantees for shared types.
- Benchmark critical paths with `cargo bench` or Criterion and profile before micro-optimizing.
- Treat warnings as errors; fail builds for unused code, dead modules, and missing `#[must_use]` where applicable.
